  "foaf:name": "Managing Biodiversity in Antarctic Marine Benthos",
  "sdo:name": "Managing Biodiversity in Antarctic Marine Benthos",
  "sdo:description": "In Antarctica, in addition to natural factors disturbing the marine communities (e.g. strong seasonality, changes in the ice sheet,...), global change is producing outstanding effects on ecosystems (increased mortality rates, invasive species, diseases, …), due to increasing sea water temperature, acidification, pollution,... Antarctica and the Southern Ocean (SO) provide ecosystem services of global importance which are key in the functioning of our planet but are still understudied. Along with regulation of climate and oceanographic systems worldwide, the SO is home to a high, unique and scarcely impacted biodiversity. Antarctic benthic assemblages are very complex, but their structure and their vulnerability to environmental changes are far from being completely understood, as well as their real biodiversity values. MANTBEN will increase the available information to be used for a better management of these threatened environments and to increase global public awareness.",
